# The truncated icosidodecahedron: the root of its system, exactly

The root of `archimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron_nu_system_0` (`Proof/Roots.lean`) written out exactly: `x i = aᵢ(β) / δ(β)` for the
elements `aᵢ` of `exactNum` and `δ = exactDelta` of `ℤ[β]`, where `β` is the root of a monic integer
polynomial of degree 52 enclosed in `exactRoot` (`Check.ZTheta`, `Modules/Check/Number/Theta.lean`).
Compiled code checks that the point lies in the system's box and solves its equations
(`exact_point_ok`), and that `nuPolynomial` vanishes at its first coordinate (`exact_uni_ok`)
(`Check.ExactPoint`, `Modules/System/ExactPoint.lean`). The system has exactly one root, of scale
`ν` (`archimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron_nu_reps_list`, `Proof/Representatives.lean`): the point is that root, and
`nuPolynomial` vanishes at `ν` (`nu_polynomial`).

Generated by `lean-new/scripts/nu_polynomial.py` from a recognition of the root in PARI/GP, which
nothing here assumes.
-/

